{"id": "RT-science-genetics-gen-04", "body": {"t": "main", "a": {"class": "wrap", "id": "main-content"}, "c": [" ", " ", {"t": "p", "a": {"class": "kicker"}, "c": ["Confirmed science / Genetics · GEN-04"]}, " ", {"t": "h1", "c": ["Common variants, rare variants and the heritability gap"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-meta"}, "c": [{"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["Last updated 30 September 2026"]}, {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["GEN-04"]}]}, " ", {"t": "details", "a": {"class": "toc", "open": "true"}, "c": [{"t": "summary", "c": ["On this page"]}, {"t": "ol", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#how-transporters-shape-a-signal"}, "c": ["How transporters shape a signal"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-needs-distinguishing"}, "c": ["What needs distinguishing"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#the-plain-english-layer"}, "c": ["The plain-English layer"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#the-deeper-layer"}, "c": ["The deeper layer"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#why-this-matters-for-how-adhd-is-described"}, "c": ["Why this matters for how ADHD is described"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-this-evidence-can-tell-us"}, "c": ["What this evidence can tell us"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#sources"}, "c": ["Sources"]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-body gen-article"}, "c": [" ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "how-transporters-shape-a-signal"}, "c": ["How transporters shape a signal"]}, " ", {"t": "ul", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": ["Twin studies say ADHD is about ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["74%"]}, " heritable ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}, "."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["Genome-wide studies say common DNA variants account for roughly ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["a third"]}, " of that ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}, "."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["The difference is not a contradiction. It is called the ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["heritability gap"]}, ", and researchers think part of it lies in rarer variants and structural changes that common-variant studies cannot see ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, ", ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-3", "aria-label": "Source 3"}, "c": ["3"]}, "]"]}, " (", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "tier tier-b"}, "c": ["Tier B"]}, ")."]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-needs-distinguishing", "class": "sec sec-misread"}, "c": ["What needs distinguishing"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["\"If the genes are not found, it must not be genetic.\" Not finding every gene is a limit of the method, not evidence against heredity. Family studies show the trait is inherited; DNA studies are still working out how."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "the-plain-english-layer"}, "c": ["The plain-English layer"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["Picture the genetic contribution as ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["many small dials plus a few large switches"]}, "."]}, " ", {"t": "ul", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Small dials:"]}, " common variants. Thousands, each adding a sliver of risk. Genome-wide association studies (", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-gwas", "title": "A study that scans the whole genome in many people to find common DNA differences linked to a trait"}, "c": ["GWAS"]}, ") are built to find these."]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Large switches:"]}, " rare variants, including ones that appear for the first time in a child (", {"t": "em", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-de-novo", "title": "New in a person, not inherited from either parent"}, "c": ["de novo"]}]}, ") and missing or extra stretches of DNA. They are harder to find because few people carry any one of them. They are found by sequencing families or very large case-control groups."]}]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "table-wrap", "role": "region", "aria-label": "Table"}, "c": [{"t": "table", "c": [{"t": "thead", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Variant type"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["How common"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Typical effect per variant"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["How it is found"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["ADHD example"]}]}]}, {"t": "tbody", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Common single-letter changes (SNPs)"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Common"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Very small"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["GWAS"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["27 ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-locus", "title": "A region of DNA"}, "c": ["loci"]}, " in 2023 ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-2", "aria-label": "Source 2"}, "c": ["2"]}, "]"]}, "; 39 in a 2025 meta-analysis that added symptom scores ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-4", "aria-label": "Source 4"}, "c": ["4"]}, "]"]}]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Rare damaging changes, including ", {"t": "em", "c": ["de novo"]}]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Rare to ultra-rare"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Larger"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Exome or genome sequencing of families and large case-control sets"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["KDM5B identified as a high-confidence risk gene ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-3", "aria-label": "Source 3"}, "c": ["3"]}, "]"]}]}]}, {"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": ["Copy-number variants (CNVs)"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Rare"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Can be large"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Microarray or sequencing"]}, {"t": "td", "c": ["Account for part of the ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-heritability", "title": "The proportion of differences in a trait across a population that is explained by genetic differences. It is not the proportion of any one person's condition"}, "c": ["heritability"]}, " ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}]}]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "the-deeper-layer"}, "c": ["The deeper layer"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["What the 2024 sequencing study did."]}, " It sequenced the exomes (the protein-coding parts of DNA) of 152 families, each with a child with ADHD and both parents, and found more rare, new, gene-damaging variants in ADHD cases than expected. It then combined these results with a case-control cohort of 3,206 people with ADHD and 5,002 controls. KDM5B emerged as a high-confidence risk gene, and the authors estimated that about ", {"t": "strong", "c": ["1,057 genes"]}, " contribute to ADHD risk. The genes they found overlap with risk genes for other neuropsychiatric conditions and are enriched in pathways that the authors say suggest early neurodevelopmental underpinnings ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-3", "aria-label": "Source 3"}, "c": ["3"]}, "]"]}, "."]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["What the 2025 meta-analysis added."]}, " Using 290,134 symptom measures from 70,953 people, then combining these with diagnosis data, it found 39 independent loci (17 new). Symptoms alone gave no genome-wide significant variants, yet combining them with diagnosis increased power. The authors read this as support for clinical ADHD sitting at the extreme end of a continuous liability ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-4", "aria-label": "Source 4"}, "c": ["4"]}, "]"]}, "."]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Why the gap may persist."]}, " The commonly proposed reasons are: rare variants and structural variants not captured by common-variant studies; the limits of twin-study assumptions; and interactions between genes and environment. These are standard explanations in the field; none is settled for ADHD specifically. (", {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "tier tier-b"}, "c": ["Tier B/C"]}, ")"]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "why-this-matters-for-how-adhd-is-described"}, "c": ["Why this matters for how ADHD is described"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["Findings of early neurodevelopmental pathways ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-3", "aria-label": "Source 3"}, "c": ["3"]}, "]"]}, " and of a continuous liability ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-4", "aria-label": "Source 4"}, "c": ["4"]}, "]"]}, " fit the classification of ADHD as a neurodevelopmental condition. The policy consequences of that are argued in the policy section of this site, not here, so that this page stays a statement of evidence."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-this-evidence-can-tell-us", "class": "sec sec-limit"}, "c": ["What this evidence can tell us"]}, " ", {"t": "ul", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": ["\"About a third\" and \"74%\" come from different kinds of study and different estimation methods. Do not subtract one from the other and call the remainder \"unknown genes\"."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["1,057 is an ", {"t": "em", "c": ["estimate of how many genes contribute"]}, ", from one study. It is not a list of 1,057 confirmed ADHD genes."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["KDM5B is a single-study high-confidence finding and should be described that way until replicated."]}, {"t": "li", "c": ["Nothing here implies that any one person's ADHD is explained by a rare variant."]}]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "sources", "class": "sec sec-src"}, "c": ["Sources"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["Bibliographic details checked against PubMed."]}, " ", {"t": "ol", "c": [{"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-1"}, "c": ["Faraone SV, Larsson H. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Mol Psychiatry"]}, " 2019;24(4):562-575. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41380-018-0070-0", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29892054/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["29892054"]}]}, {"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-2"}, "c": ["Demontis D et al. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Nat Genet"]}, " 2023. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-022-01285-8", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36702997/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["36702997"]}]}, {"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-3"}, "c": ["Olfson E et al. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Nat Commun"]}, " 2024;15:5870. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-50247-7", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38997333/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["38997333"]}]}, {"t": "li", "a": {"id": "src-4"}, "c": ["van der Laan CM et al. ", {"t": "em", "c": ["Nat Genet"]}, " 2025;57(10):2427-2435. ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41588-025-02295-y", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["DOI"]}, " · PMID ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40962958/", "rel": "noopener"}, "c": ["40962958"]}]}]}, " "]}, " ", {"t": "p", "a": {"class": "gloss-hint"}, "c": ["Underlined terms link to the ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/"}, "c": ["glossary"]}, "; hover or long-press for a quick definition."]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "nextbox"}, "c": [{"t": "strong", "c": ["Useful next destination."]}, " ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-05/"}, "c": ["GEN-05"]}, ": Polygenic scores: what they can and cannot do."]}, " ", {"t": "nav", "a": {"class": "gen-series", "aria-label": "Genetics series"}, "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/"}, "c": ["All genetics articles"]}, {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/"}, "c": ["Glossary"]}, {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/sources/numbers/"}, "c": ["Verified numbers"]}]}, " "]}}